g","mtime":"1733257061","size":"14984","md5":"72167c91b8c1620fbe3b591bcf75f502","crc32":"9fa3507a","sha1":"157b359070811ea93ffec4389a22cd78d02d0038"},{"name":"__ia_thumb.jpg","source":"original","mtime":"1733255315","size":"21578","md5":"803023885ea63c970fc4f91b40be3cc9","crc32":"071bfd9f","sha1":"01d78f00c06fe3d2f43ed6791ec76fd3e2aa0f3a","format":"Item Tile"},{"name":"alexand-chrissy-bb-e-03-mixdown_archive.torrent","source":"metadata","btih":"923d40307885916127dae6cfa41fbf1c011441f0","mtime":"1733257535","size":"4674","md5":"4c777092adc57218b5e154bd312693fe","crc32":"d41fcf55","sha1":"79bb96f587e0387201bf0aa76125a533e9bb7389","format":"Archive BitTorrent"},{"name":"alexand-chrissy-bb-e-03-mixdown_files.xml","source":"original","format":"Metadata","md5":"35066b3125c702ce234446f58b47e6ac","summation":"md5"},{"name":"alexand-chrissy-bb-e-03-mixdown_meta.sqlite","source":"original","mtime":"1733255280","size":"49152","md5":"4dc368945b7740a2c8357c34e25800f6","crc32":"885989fe","sha1":"12ff009ae3d9d13f04cb30c88164f420f244d616","format":"Metadata"},{"name":"alexand-chrissy-bb-e-03-mixdown_meta.xml","source":"original","mtime":"1733257507","size":"4444","md5":"227b183d82fb7b6d0eb4f771787f5fe6","crc32":"27698769","sha1":"45d788b33498f7184e2de0f04a23810ca8882e87","format":"Metadata"}],"files_count":11,"item_last_updated":1733257535,"item_size":44845539,"metadata":{"identifier":"alexand-chrissy-bb-e-03-mixdown","mediatype":"audio","collection":["du-participatory-archive","audio_music"],"creator":"Gus Baxter","date":"2024-12-03","description":"In this special episode of The Bravery Blueprint, host Gus Baxter is joined by twins Alex and Chrissy Pollock, Drew University alumni who share their insights on success and personal growth. Alex, a deputy editor with a background in psychology and Italian, and Chrissy, a medical malpractice claims consultant with a double major in psychology and Italian, discuss how their liberal arts education shaped their careers and personal lives. Reflecting on their college experiences, Alex and Chrissy offer advice on embracing risks and being open to new opportunities. They emphasize the importance of following one's passions, being adaptable, and trusting the process, even when the path seems unclear. They also address common college anxieties, such as the pressure to make the \"right\" choices and the value of networking, stressing that personal growth often involves navigating discomfort and adjusting plans as needed. Through their stories, they highlight how the skills and relationships built during their time at Drew University, including strong faculty connections and the ability to pivot, have been crucial in their professional journeys. They encourage listeners to remain open to learning and evolving, and to trust their own instincts in pursuing their goals.<div><br /></div><div><b>CREDITS</b></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);\"><br /></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);\">The Bravery Blueprint is hosted &amp; written by Gust Baxter with theme music and audio engineering by Logan Flores</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);\"><br /></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);\">To learn more about Drew University's Center for Career Development visit: </span><a href=\"https://drew.edu/academic/student-resources/center-for-career-development/\" style=\"background:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(75,100,255);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://drew.edu/academic/student-